Absolute [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Sets the Time Reference of the TimeSequence designated by <Path> to Absolute (true) or Relative
(false).
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Absolute:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyTimeSequence.Absolute := true
See also
Time Reference [TimeSequence]
Absolute [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Plant Simulation Help 11-4327
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Active [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Activates the object designated by <Path> (true), i.e., makes it record data, or deactivates it (false).
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Active:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyTimeSequence.Active := true
See also
Active [check box] - TimeSequence
Active [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
11-4328 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

DefaultValue [SimTalk]
Sets the Default Value of the TimeSequence designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The data type of the TimeSequence matches the data type of the column Value on the tab Contents of
the TimeSequence.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.DefaultValue:any
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type any.
Example
MyTimeSequence.DefaultValue := "Body"
See also
Default Value [TimeSequence]
DefaultValue [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4329
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Path [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Sets the Path to the value which the TimeSequence designated by <Path> is to record.
Remarks
The value can be specified as a relative or as an absolute path.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Path:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
Example
MyTimeSequence.Path := "Station.NumMU"
MyTimeSequence.Path := "&MyVariable"
See also
Value [TimeSequence]
Path [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
11-4330 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

ReferenceDate [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Sets the offset value of the time sequence inputs for the setting Time Reference > Absolute of the
TimeSequence designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation adds it to each time value in the TimeSequence table. By changing the reference time,
you can shift the values in time without re-entering the data.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ReferenceDate:dateTime
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type dateTime.
Example
ts1.ReferenceDate := sysdate
See also
Start Date [Trigger]
ReferenceDate [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Plant Simulation Help 11-4331
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

ReferenceTime [SimTalk] - TimeSequence
Sets the Start Time of the TimeSequence designated by <Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ReferenceTime:time
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type time.
Example
ts1.ReferenceTime := str_to_time("1:00:00:00.00")
See also
Start Time [Trigger]
